// LLD of the service namespace (ds::service, DS-406, DS-407): the use cases of DriftSpec (design/usecases.ds), each
// a class realising a small interface whose operation realises its UC, so the trace runs from the use case to the
// class. A use case is given the loaded model, a request and the sink its door lends it; it computes its document as
// a local value, describes it into the sink through DescriptionFactory and says how it ended, in one of the outcomes
// its UC declares. It knows no door: the command line, the engine, the browser and the Python face translate its
// outcome and its failures, each to its own convention (DS-409). UseCaseFactory is the one place naming them.

package driftspec@ds {

  requirement REQ-00261-1 {
    status: draft
    @refines REQ-00107-2
    title: The engine shall serve each use case of DriftSpec behind one interface, made by one factory, describing its document into the sink its door lends and ending in an outcome its use case declares
    text:
      A use case of design/usecases.ds is one class: check-design, see-design, ask-model, hand-model,
      learn-language and edit-design. Each realises a small interface whose operation realises its UC, and all
      are IUseCase: name(), needs(bound model, request), the check steps it reads, and run(model, request,
      lent sink) -> Outcome, which fails BadRequest for a request that is not its own and NotImplemented for what
      the sink's technology cannot write. A use case describes its document into the sink it is lent, through
      DescriptionFactory, and returns one of the outcomes its UC declares; the outcomes that happen before a model
      exists (bad-usage, no-workspace) are the door's. UseCaseFactory is the one place naming a use case. What a
      use case describes is byte for byte what its door writes of the same document.
    rationale: Owner, 2026-11-24 (DS-406, the service layer; sketch proposal-service v4); code-62, 2026-11-25 (DS-407, D1 needs reads the bound model and the request, D2 the door's outcomes stay at the door, D3 the text forms join after DS-399).
    tags: service, use-cases
    verification VER-00281-1 {
      status: draft
      title: Integration tests confirm each use case describes what its door writes byte for byte, ends in an outcome its use case declares, and is made by the factory alone
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/service/test_use_cases.cpp::TestUseCases.EachUseCaseDescribesWhatItsDoorWritesByteForByte
        tests/integration/ds/service/test_use_cases.cpp::TestUseCases.EachUseCaseEndsInAnOutcomeItsUseCaseDeclares
        tests/integration/ds/service/test_use_cases.cpp::TestUseCases.TheFactoryNamesEveryUseCaseAndAnyOtherNameIsNotImplemented
        tests/integration/ds/service/test_use_cases.cpp::TestUseCases.ARequestThatIsNotTheUseCasesIsABadRequestAndADrawingTakesOnlyWhatItReads
    }
  }

  requirement REQ-00301-1 {
    status: draft
    @refines REQ-00261-1
    title: The see-design use case shall draw a workspace's diagram in svg and text, describe its render-IR and write the viewer's page framed on a diagram, so that no door draws
    text:
      see-design is asked a format and what the format needs, and is the one place a workspace is drawn: the
      scene (json); the viewer's page (html), framed on what the diagram asked shows, or on the identities of
      focus, titled, with a reader's stylesheet, embedded and how tall as asked; a diagram's layout, cells and
      render-IR, described into the sink lent; and its drawing in svg or in text, wrapped to the width asked and
      in colour when asked, drawn through render and handed to the sink as a verbatim text, as is the page. A
      diagram the workspace lacks ends in no-diagram, saying it, and so does a page framed on one. Asked whole,
      as the command line asks, a diagram is not drawn of what did not read whole (DS-433): when a file of its
      own, or of what it shows, does not parse or is not UTF-8, or when it is missing or shows nothing while a
      file of the workspace does not read whole, it ends in no-diagram and the outcome says each such finding as
      ds check does, then why it is not drawn. Not asked whole, as the engine's interfaces ask, it draws what it
      can. A format that is none of these fails NotImplemented. What see-design writes is byte for byte what the
      door wrote of the same diagram, page and IR.
    rationale:
      DS-474 (from DS-409's CLI half, agreed with code-62, 2026-11-25): the command line still drew svg, text
      and the IR at the door, over the workspace's model, and read the viewer's focus and DS-433's unread files
      there too. Coordinator, 2026-11-25: the drawings reach the sink as a verbatim text, a bridge until DS-463
      describes a figure as marks; the unread-file check runs only when the request asks it whole, so an
      editor's preview of a diagram whose file is broken mid-edit still draws, as it always did.
    tags: service, use-cases, render
    verification VER-00322-1 {
      status: draft
      title: Integration tests confirm see-design draws every diagram of the golden workspaces in svg and text and describes its IR byte for byte as ds render wrote them, writes the viewer's page, and says a diagram that is missing or did not read whole
      method: test
      tests:
        tests/integration/ds/service/test_use_cases.cpp::TestUseCases.SeeDesignDrawsEveryDiagramAsDsRenderWroteIt
        tests/integration/ds/service/test_use_cases.cpp::TestUseCases.SeeDesignWritesTheViewersPageFramedOnADiagram
        tests/integration/ds/service/test_use_cases.cpp::TestUseCases.SeeDesignAskedWholeSaysADiagramThatDidNotReadWhole
    }
  }

  interface check-design {
    kind: library
    transport: in process, linked
    operation report(model: model::Model) -> check::Report : UC-00001-1 {
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
    }
  }

  interface see-design {
    kind: library
    transport: in process, linked
    operation viewer(model: model::Model) -> scene::SceneDocument : UC-00002-1 {
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
    }
  }

  interface ask-model {
    kind: library
    transport: in process, linked
    operation ask(model: model::Model, question: std::string, subject: std::string) -> std::vector<query::Answer> : UC-00004-1 {
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
    }
  }

  interface hand-model {
    kind: library
    transport: in process, linked
    operation run(model: model::Model, request: service::Request, sink: emit::ISink) -> service::Outcome fails BadRequest, emit::NotImplemented : UC-00005-1 {
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
    }
  }

  interface learn-language {
    kind: library
    transport: in process, linked
    operation page(topic: std::string) -> std::string : UC-00006-1 {
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
    }
  }

  interface edit-design {
    kind: library
    transport: in process, linked
    operation expectedAt(text: std::string, line: int, column: int) -> std::vector<std::string> : UC-00007-1 {
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
    }
  }

  // how each operation is handled: by its use case's class. The outcomes that happen before a model exists (bad-usage,
  // no-workspace) are the door's (DS-407, D2) and are handled where the door is (DS-409)
  sequence check-design::report {
    local checks: service::CheckDesign
    -> checks.report(model) -> report
    return report
  }

  sequence check-design::report / errors {          // an error is among the findings: the report says where
    local checks: service::CheckDesign
    -> checks.report(model) -> report
    return report
  }

  sequence see-design::viewer {
    local sees: service::SeeDesign
    -> sees.viewer(model) -> document
    return document
  }

  sequence see-design::viewer / no-diagram {         // the diagram named is not in the workspace, or asked whole did not read whole: nothing is drawn
    local sees: service::SeeDesign
    -> sees.unread(model, name, workspace) -> why
    -> sees.diagram(model, name) -> ir
    return ir
  }

  sequence ask-model::ask {
    local asks: service::AskModel
    -> asks.ask(model, question, subject) -> answers
    return answers
  }

  sequence ask-model::ask / unknown-question {       // the question, or its subject, is not one the model answers
    local asks: service::AskModel
    -> asks.ask(model, question, subject) -> answers
    return answers
  }

  sequence hand-model::run {
    local hands: service::HandModel
    -> hands.run(model, request, sink) -> outcome
    return outcome
  }

  sequence learn-language::page {
    local teaches: service::LearnLanguage
    -> teaches.page(topic) -> text
    return text
  }

  sequence learn-language::page / no-topic {         // no such page: the outcome lists the topics, and the door says them
    local teaches: service::LearnLanguage
    -> teaches.page(topic) -> text
    return text
  }

  sequence edit-design::expectedAt {
    local edits: service::EditDesign
    -> edits.expectedAt(text, line, column) -> words
    return words
  }

  module service {
    @requirement REQ-00261-1

    // what a use case is asked: its arguments by name (the diagram, the question, the topic, the line...), each a text,
    // read as it is, as a whole number, as a flag or as lines
    class Request {
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
      @requirement REQ-00301-1
      + arguments: std::map<std::string, std::string>
      + get(name: std::string) -> std::string fails BadRequest
      + getOr(name: std::string, fallback: std::string) -> std::string
      + number(name: std::string, fallback: std::string) -> int fails BadRequest   // a whole number, or BadRequest
      + flag(name: std::string) -> bool                  // "true"; false when not given
      + lines(name: std::string) -> std::vector<std::string>   // its items, each ended by a line break (the last may not be)
    }

    // how a use case ended: one of the outcomes its UC declares, and for any but default what happened, in a line, which
    // each door words in its own convention: the command line writes it on stderr (DS-409)
    dataclass Outcome {
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
      + name: std::string
      + message: std::string
    }

    // a request that is not the use case's: an argument it needs and is not given, or one it cannot read
    class BadRequest : std::invalid_argument {
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
    }

    // THE COMMON INTERFACE: what the doors and the workspace ask of any use case, by name
    class IUseCase {
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
      + ~IUseCase()
      + abstract name() -> std::string
      + abstract needs(bound: model::Model, request: Request) -> check::Selection
      + abstract run(model: model::Model, request: Request, sink: emit::ISink) -> Outcome fails BadRequest, emit::NotImplemented
    }

    class CheckDesign : IUseCase {                      // UC-00001-1: check a design
      @interface check-design
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
      - refs metamodel_: model::Metamodel
      + CheckDesign(metamodel: model::Metamodel)
      + report(model: model::Model) -> check::Report
      + name() -> std::string
      + needs(bound: model::Model, request: Request) -> check::Selection
      + run(model: model::Model, request: Request, sink: emit::ISink) -> Outcome fails BadRequest, emit::NotImplemented
    }

    // UC-00002-1: see the design, the viewer's scene or its page, or a diagram drawn; every drawing of a workspace is
    // drawn here (DS-474), so no door draws. Its request contract, the arguments it reads:
    //   format     json (the scene) · html (the viewer's page) · ir, layout, cells, svg, text (a diagram); any other is
    //              NotImplemented
    //   diagram    the diagram drawn; for html, the one the page is framed on (what it shows), no-diagram when none
    //   focus      html: the identities the page is framed on, one a line, when no diagram is named
    //   title, css, embed, height   html: the page's title, a reader's stylesheet, an iframe that carries it, how tall
    //   width      a diagram: wrapped to it, columns for text and cells, pixels for svg; 0 lets it be
    //   color      text: true for a terminal that shows colour
    //   whole      a diagram: true asks it drawn only of what read whole (DS-433), as the command line asks; then a
    //              file of its own or of what it shows that did not read whole, or one of the workspace when it is
    //              missing or shows nothing, ends it in no-diagram, the outcome saying each finding and why, naming
    //   workspace  the workspace as its door was given it. Not asked whole, it draws what it can, as an editor asks.
    // The structure is described into the sink lent; a drawing and the page are handed to it as one verbatim text.
    class SeeDesign : IUseCase {
      @interface see-design
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
      @requirement REQ-00301-1
      - refs metamodel_: model::Metamodel
      - owns theme_: theme::Theme                       // the style its drawings are measured and drawn in (DS-393)
      + SeeDesign(metamodel: model::Metamodel)
      + viewer(model: model::Model) -> scene::SceneDocument
      + diagram(model: model::Model, name: std::string) -> std::optional<render::IrDocument>   // the IR as a value; none when no such diagram (DS-418)
      + unread(model: model::Model, name: std::string, workspace: std::string) -> std::string   // what it reads that did not read whole (DS-433); "" when it read whole
      + name() -> std::string
      + needs(bound: model::Model, request: Request) -> check::Selection
      // what escapes it: a request it cannot read, a format it does not write, a document its sink does not write
      // (NotImplemented, as emit's sink and description say it), a diagram of a kind render does not draw, a second
      // verbatim text
      + run(model: model::Model, request: Request, sink: emit::ISink) -> Outcome fails BadRequest, emit::NotImplemented, NotImplemented, std::invalid_argument, std::logic_error
      - page(model: model::Model, request: Request, sink: emit::ISink) -> Outcome fails BadRequest, NotImplemented, std::logic_error   // the viewer's page, a verbatim text
      - drawn(model: model::Model, format: std::string, request: Request, sink: emit::ISink) -> Outcome fails BadRequest, NotImplemented, std::invalid_argument, std::logic_error
      - static formats() -> std::vector<std::string>    // the formats it is asked in, for a message
    }

    class AskModel : IUseCase {                         // UC-00004-1: ask the model
      @interface ask-model
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
      - refs metamodel_: model::Metamodel
      + AskModel(metamodel: model::Metamodel)
      + ask(model: model::Model, question: std::string, subject: std::string) -> std::vector<query::Answer>
      + name() -> std::string
      + needs(bound: model::Model, request: Request) -> check::Selection
      + run(model: model::Model, request: Request, sink: emit::ISink) -> Outcome fails BadRequest, emit::NotImplemented
    }

    class HandModel : IUseCase {                        // UC-00005-1: hand the model to another tool
      @interface hand-model
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
      - refs metamodel_: model::Metamodel
      + HandModel(metamodel: model::Metamodel)
      + name() -> std::string
      + needs(bound: model::Model, request: Request) -> check::Selection
      + run(model: model::Model, request: Request, sink: emit::ISink) -> Outcome fails BadRequest, emit::NotImplemented
    }

    class LearnLanguage : IUseCase {                    // UC-00006-1: learn the language; it reads no design
      @interface learn-language
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
      - refs metamodel_: model::Metamodel
      + LearnLanguage(metamodel: model::Metamodel)
      + page(topic: std::string) -> std::string
      + name() -> std::string
      + needs(bound: model::Model, request: Request) -> check::Selection
      + run(model: model::Model, request: Request, sink: emit::ISink) -> Outcome fails BadRequest, emit::NotImplemented
    }

    class EditDesign : IUseCase {                       // UC-00007-1: what the editor asks the engine; it reads no model
      @interface edit-design
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
      + expectedAt(text: std::string, line: int, column: int) -> std::vector<std::string>
      + name() -> std::string
      + needs(bound: model::Model, request: Request) -> check::Selection
      + run(model: model::Model, request: Request, sink: emit::ISink) -> Outcome fails BadRequest, emit::NotImplemented
    }

    // every format is asked here: the scene described, the page and a diagram each handled by its own member; one that
    // is none of them is a pair ds does not write
    sequence SeeDesign::run {
      opt a format it does not write / unknown {
        -> formats() -> there
        fail emit::NotImplemented
      }
      alt the scene / json {
        -> viewer(model) -> document
        -> format::DescriptionFactory::scene(document) -> description
        -> description.describe(sink)
      } else {
        alt the page / html {
          -> page(model, request, sink) -> outcome
        } else {
          -> drawn(model, format, request, sink) -> outcome
        }
      }
      return outcome
    }

    // the page is the scene in JSON inside its template (DS-126): the scene and the focus travel compact inside it,
    // written into a sink of their own, and the page, written whole, is handed to the sink lent as it is
    sequence SeeDesign::page {
      local query: query::IQuery
      local html: format::IFormat<scene::SceneDocument>   // the page FormatFactory finds by name
      -> request.lines(focus) -> framed
      opt framed on a diagram / framed {
        -> query::QueryFactory::of(model, metamodel_) -> query
        -> query.ask(question, diagram) -> shown
        opt no such diagram / no-diagram {
          return noDiagram
        }
      }
      -> request.flag(embed) -> embedded
      -> request.number(height, fallback) -> tall
      -> emit::SinkFactory::json(false) -> inside
      -> viewer(model) -> document
      -> format::FormatFactory::scene() -> writers
      -> html.write(document, options, inside) -> page
      -> sink.verbatim(page)
      return drawn
    }

    // a diagram is its IR (DS-126), handed as a document to what draws it (DS-458): its IR, layout and cells described
    // into the sink lent, its drawing in svg or text drawn through render and handed to the sink as it is, a bridge
    // until a figure is described as marks (DS-463)
    sequence SeeDesign::drawn {
      local svg: render::Svg
      local text: render::Text
      -> request.get(diagram) -> name
      opt asked whole, as the command line asks (DS-433) / whole {
        -> unread(model, name, workspace) -> why
      }
      -> diagram(model, name) -> ir
      alt its IR / ir {
        -> format::DescriptionFactory::ir(ir) -> description
        -> description.describe(sink)
      } else {
        -> request.number(width, fallback) -> wide
        alt its layout or its cells / described {
          -> format::DescriptionFactory::layout(ir, theme_, wide) -> description
          -> description.describe(sink)
        } else {
          alt in svg / svg {
            -> svg.render(ir, wide) -> drawing
          } else {
            -> request.flag(color) -> coloured
            -> text.render(ir, coloured, wide) -> drawing
          }
          -> sink.verbatim(drawing)
        }
      }
      return drawn
    }

    sequence SeeDesign::drawn / no-diagram {          // no such diagram, or asked whole, one that did not read whole
      -> request.get(diagram) -> name
      -> unread(model, name, workspace) -> why
      -> diagram(model, name) -> ir
      return noDiagram
    }

    // what a diagram reads: its own file and those of what it shows; what did not read whole among them is said as ds
    // check says it
    sequence SeeDesign::unread {
      local query: query::IQuery
      -> model.find(id) -> diagram
      -> query::QueryFactory::of(model, metamodel_) -> query
      -> query.ask(question, name) -> shown
      -> model.findings() -> findings
      return said
    }

    // THE ONE PLACE THAT NAMES THE USE CASES: a door, or the workspace, asks for one by its name
    class UseCaseFactory {                  // made over the metamodel and aggregated by what asks it (DS-408)
      @requirement REQ-00261-1
      - refs metamodel_: model::Metamodel
      + UseCaseFactory(metamodel: model::Metamodel)
      + of(name: std::string) -> std::unique_ptr<IUseCase> fails emit::NotImplemented
      + metamodel() -> model::Metamodel
      + static names() -> std::vector<std::string>
    }
  }
}
